Most DevOps engineers fail these Linux questions.

1. How do you trace the system calls a process is making — in real time?
When an app hangs, logs lie. But syscalls don’t.

strace -p <PID>

⸻

2. How do you find which process is writing to a file — live — without killing anything?
The log keeps changing. But who’s writing to it?

lsof | grep /path/to/file.log

⸻

3. How do you throttle CPU usage of a process — without stopping it?
Production server. High load. You can’t kill it. What now?

cpulimit -p <PID> -l 30

⸻

4. How do you permanently restrict memory or CPU usage for a container or service using cgroups?
No Docker flags. Just real Linux resource control.

cgcreate -g memory,cpu:/mygroup 
cgset -r memory.limit_in_bytes=500M mygroup 
cgexec -g memory,cpu:mygroup ./your_script.sh

